# Credentials for defender/agents/langchain_registry.py (llm_soc's LLMAgent /
# SysFlowAgent). Copy to `.env` at the repo root and fill in the values; `.env`
# itself is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# The defender picks a model through the harness's llm_soc plugin `llm_model`
# field. Three prefixes choose the route; anything else falls back to the fixed
# model table in LangChainRegistry.
#
#   anthropic/<model>        -> first-party Anthropic API   (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY)
#   openrouter/<model-slug>  -> OpenRouter                  (OPENROUTER_API_KEY)
#   litellm/<model>          -> CMU LiteLLM gateway         (LITELLM_API_KEY + LITELLM_BASE_URL)
#
# All three log per-call input/output/cache tokens, wall-clock latency, the
# served model id, and a dollar cost to <output_dir>/token_usage.json. Cost
# provenance differs: OpenRouter returns it in the response body, LiteLLM in the
# x-litellm-response-cost header, and the Anthropic API returns none at all - so
# for `anthropic/...` it is computed from token counts x the list prices in
# LangChainRegistry._ANTHROPIC_PRICES_PER_MTOK. That table is a snapshot; update
# it when Anthropic's published prices change, or the figures will drift.

# ---- Direct first-party Anthropic API -> enables the "anthropic/<model>" prefix.
# e.g. llm_model = anthropic/claude-sonnet-5
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=''

# ---- OpenRouter -> enables the "openrouter/<model-slug>" prefix.
# The only route serving BOTH claude-sonnet-4.5 and claude-sonnet-5, so a
# 4.5-vs-5 defender comparison must keep both arms here (the CMU LiteLLM gateway
# has no 4.5). Optional: OPENROUTER_BASE_URL overrides the default endpoint.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=''

# ---- CMU LiteLLM gateway -> enables the "litellm/<model>" prefix. Both required.
LITELLM_API_KEY=''
LITELLM_BASE_URL=''

# ---- Unused by the prefixed routes above. Needed only for the fixed model-table
# names that call a provider SDK directly (gpt-4o, gemini-2.5-pro, ...).
OPENAI_API_KEY=''
GOOGLE_API_KEY=''
